// The missing semicolon is on the last line, and that is where the diagnostic has
// to point.
//
// The unit-wide terminator the parser reads at end of file used to be built by
// zeroing a token, so its position was 0:0 and this came out as "line 0" quoting
// the first line of the file -- which, in a file that opens with a comment, points
// at the one line that has nothing to do with it.
var greeting = "hi";
print(greeting + ", its me")
